Disclaimer: Pulsar is a fork of pactl-gui, originally written by Skrappjaw.
 The MIT license text is reproduced in full below rather than referenced from
 the common-licenses index, because upstream pactl-gui states in its README
 that it is MIT licensed but publishes no LICENSE file. There is therefore no
 upstream file for this package to point a License: field at, so the text is
 carried inline and attributed to its source.
Comment:
 Pulsar is a derivative work of pactl-gui (https://github.com/Skrappjaw/
 pactl-gui). Some of the code in this package originates in that project and
 remains the copyright of its original author. Both Pulsar's own code and the
 inherited pactl-gui code are distributed under the MIT license, which is why
 a single license block covers both copyright holders below.
 .
 The two copyright holders are listed together in one stanza rather than
 split into per-file stanzas. Which files descend from pactl-gui and which are
 new in Pulsar has never been recorded at the file level upstream, and
 guessing at a split would produce a machine-readable claim that is not
 accurate. A single stanza covering all files with both holders is the
 honest, if less precise, representation; both holders consented to the same
 terms, so the license grant itself is unambiguous either way.
